WEBVTT

00:00:08.803 --> 00:00:10.310
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:10.316 --> 00:00:11.885
Let's say good night to your brother.

00:00:12.088 --> 00:00:13.148
Night, Sam.

00:00:13.272 --> 00:00:14.652
Hey, Dean.

00:00:14.677 --> 00:00:16.206
Daddy! Hey, buddy.

00:00:17.127 --> 00:00:18.734
Sweet dreams, Sam.

00:00:22.892 --> 00:00:25.370
Dad's missing. I need
you to help me find him.

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:27.317
The trail for dad, it's getting colder.

00:00:27.441 --> 00:00:30.031
Every day. You don't think I want
to find dad as much as you do?

00:00:30.055 --> 00:00:31.433
I know you do. Find dad.

00:00:31.457 --> 00:00:33.750
Mom's gone. She isn't coming back.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.151
Don't talk about her like that.

00:01:01.344 --> 00:01:02.599
Mommy?

00:01:04.259 --> 00:01:06.188
Hey, sweetie.

00:01:06.464 --> 00:01:10.413
Why aren't you in bed?
There's something in my closet.

00:01:26.231 --> 00:01:27.071
See?

00:01:27.106 --> 00:01:28.385
There's nothing there.

00:01:29.763 --> 00:01:32.702
You're sure? I'm sure.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:40.990
Now, come on.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.101
Into bed.

00:01:49.544 --> 00:01:51.167
I don't like this house.

00:01:51.782 --> 00:01:53.381
You're just not used to it yet.

00:01:54.190 --> 00:02:00.045
But you and your brother and me,
we are going to be very happy here.

00:02:00.596 --> 00:02:01.604
I promise.

00:02:04.209 --> 00:02:05.864
I love you.

00:02:13.664 --> 00:02:14.417
The chair.

00:02:15.299 --> 00:02:16.712
Okay.

00:02:17.351 --> 00:02:18.329
Right.

00:02:22.204 --> 00:02:23.258
The chair.

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:27.572
Just to be safe.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:03.348
Please, god, don't let it be rats.

00:03:23.057 --> 00:03:24.294
Terrific.

00:05:21.885 --> 00:05:22.578
All right.

00:05:22.603 --> 00:05:24.400
I've been cruising some websites.

00:05:24.505 --> 00:05:26.899
Think I found a few
candidates for our next gig.

00:05:28.206 --> 00:05:30.963
A fishing trawler found
off the coast of Cali.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:32.486
Its crew vanished.

00:05:32.717 --> 00:05:36.200
And we got some cattle
mutilations in west Texas.

00:05:36.682 --> 00:05:37.299
Hey!

00:05:39.131 --> 00:05:41.193
Am I boring you with
this hunting-Evil stuff?

00:05:41.733 --> 00:05:43.815
No, I'm listening. Keep going.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:48.596
And here a Sacramento man
shot himself in the head...

00:05:49.039 --> 00:05:50.273
Three times.

00:05:52.711 --> 00:05:54.754
Any of these things
blowing up your skirt, pal?

00:05:58.783 --> 00:06:00.817
Wait, I've seen this. Seen what?

00:06:07.678 --> 00:06:08.791
What are you doing?

00:06:17.132 --> 00:06:18.872
Dean, I know where we have to go next.

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:19.584
Where?

00:06:20.213 --> 00:06:21.151
Back home.

00:06:21.965 --> 00:06:22.989
Back to Kansas.

00:06:24.383 --> 00:06:26.258
Okay, random. Where'd that come from?

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:28.152
All right, um...

00:06:28.192 --> 00:06:30.521
This photo was taken in
front of our old house, right?

00:06:30.606 --> 00:06:31.821
The house where mom died?

00:06:33.266 --> 00:06:33.922
Yeah.

00:06:33.999 --> 00:06:37.161
It didn't burn down right? I mean not
completely, they rebuilt it, right?

00:06:37.238 --> 00:06:39.590
I guess so, yeah. What the
hell are you talking about?

00:06:39.621 --> 00:06:41.831
Okay, look, this is gonna sound crazy,

00:06:41.861 --> 00:06:43.944
But the people who
live in our old house,

00:06:45.212 --> 00:06:46.851
I think they might be in danger.

00:06:47.196 --> 00:06:49.566
Why would you think that? Uh...

00:06:49.624 --> 00:06:51.646
Just, um... look, just...

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:53.030
You got to trust me on this, okay?

00:06:54.667 --> 00:06:56.736
Hey, whoa, whoa, whoa. Trust you? Yeah.

00:06:57.254 --> 00:06:59.158
You got to give me a
little bit more than that.

00:06:59.204 --> 00:07:00.936
I can't really explain, it is all.

00:07:01.141 --> 00:07:03.665
Well, tough. I'm not going
anywhere until you do.

00:07:08.327 --> 00:07:10.023
I have these nightmares.

00:07:10.324 --> 00:07:11.728
I've noticed.

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:16.514
And sometimes they come true.

00:07:19.566 --> 00:07:20.574
Come again?

00:07:21.437 --> 00:07:22.116
Look, Dean...

00:07:23.309 --> 00:07:24.773
I dreamt about Jessica's death

00:07:25.572 --> 00:07:27.484
For days before it happened.

00:07:30.083 --> 00:07:32.827
Sane people have weird dreams, man.
I'm sure it's just a coincidence.

00:07:33.376 --> 00:07:36.510
No, I dreamt about the blood dripping,
her on the ceiling, the fire, everything,

00:07:36.522 --> 00:07:38.389
And I didn't do anything
'cause I didn't believe it.

00:07:38.447 --> 00:07:40.067
Now I'm dreaming about that tree,

00:07:40.236 --> 00:07:43.087
About our house, and some woman
inside screaming for help. I mean,

00:07:43.276 --> 00:07:45.716
That's where it all started, man.
This has to mean something, right?

00:07:47.991 --> 00:07:48.824
I don't know.

00:07:49.844 --> 00:07:52.025
What do you mean you
don't know, Dean? This...

00:07:52.143 --> 00:07:53.832
This woman might be in danger.

00:07:53.891 --> 00:07:58.031
This might be the thing that killed mom and
Jessica. All right, just slow down,would you?

00:08:02.066 --> 00:08:04.670
I mean, first you're telling
me that you've got this Shining

00:08:05.879 --> 00:08:07.756
and then you tell me that
I've got to go back home,

00:08:08.999 --> 00:08:09.922
Especially when...

00:08:11.905 --> 00:08:13.009
When what?

00:08:14.427 --> 00:08:16.714
When I swore to myself that
I would never go back there.

00:08:28.115 --> 00:08:30.062
Dean, we have to check this out.

00:08:31.208 --> 00:08:32.608
Just to make sure.

00:08:39.936 --> 00:08:41.027
I know we do.

00:08:59.466 --> 00:09:01.066
You gonna be all right, man?

00:09:02.967 --> 00:09:04.793
Let me get back to you on that.

00:09:12.865 --> 00:09:13.358
Yes?

00:09:13.628 --> 00:09:14.988
Sorry to bother you, ma'am,

00:09:15.099 --> 00:09:17.492
But we're with the
federal... I'm Sam Winchester

00:09:17.726 --> 00:09:19.486
And this is my brother, Dean.

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:21.884
Um...we used to live here.

00:09:22.799 --> 00:09:25.169
You know, we were just driving by, and

00:09:25.222 --> 00:09:27.603
We were wondering if we
could come see the old place.

00:09:27.664 --> 00:09:28.825
Winchester...

00:09:30.362 --> 00:09:31.817
That is so funny.

00:09:32.013 --> 00:09:35.333
You know, I, I think I found some
of your photos the other night.

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:36.025
You did?

00:09:40.291 --> 00:09:42.441
Okay. Come on in.

00:09:54.381 --> 00:09:56.446
Juice, juice, juice!

00:09:56.481 --> 00:09:58.399
Juice, juice,  juice!

00:09:58.422 --> 00:10:02.293
That's Richie. He's
kind of a juice junkie.

00:10:02.532 --> 00:10:05.499
But, hey, at least he won't get scurvy.

00:10:06.755 --> 00:10:07.857
Sari,

00:10:08.268 --> 00:10:10.368
This is Sam and Dean.

00:10:10.416 --> 00:10:12.351
They used to live here. Hi.

00:10:12.879 --> 00:10:13.817
Hey, Sari.

00:10:14.768 --> 00:10:16.070
So, you just moved in?

00:10:16.128 --> 00:10:17.853
Uh, yeah, from Wichita.

00:10:17.955 --> 00:10:19.375
You got family here?

00:10:20.466 --> 00:10:22.436
No, I just, uh...

00:10:23.598 --> 00:10:26.759
Um, needed a fresh start. That's all.

00:10:27.888 --> 00:10:30.089
So new town,

00:10:30.199 --> 00:10:31.317
New job

00:10:31.501 --> 00:10:33.333
I mean, as soon as I find one,

00:10:33.737 --> 00:10:35.001
New house.

00:10:37.056 --> 00:10:38.816
So, how you liking it so far?

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:43.783
Well, uh, all due respect
to your childhood home,

00:10:43.875 --> 00:10:47.320
I mean, I'm sure you have
lots of happy memories here,

00:10:47.778 --> 00:10:50.051
But this place has its issues.

00:10:50.326 --> 00:10:51.536
What do you mean?

00:10:52.909 --> 00:10:54.706
Well, it's just getting old

00:10:55.109 --> 00:10:57.235
Like, the wiring, you know? We've got

00:10:57.363 --> 00:10:59.471
Flickering lights almost hourly.

00:10:59.581 --> 00:11:00.827
Oh, that's too bad.

00:11:01.304 --> 00:11:02.330
What else?

00:11:02.678 --> 00:11:06.986
Um...sink's backed up.
There's rats in the basement.

00:11:09.096 --> 00:11:10.526
I'm sorry.

00:11:10.691 --> 00:11:12.798
I don't mean to complain. No.

00:11:12.872 --> 00:11:16.262
Have you seen the rats or
have you just heard scratching?

00:11:17.344 --> 00:11:20.386
Just the scratching, actually. Mom?

00:11:24.784 --> 00:11:27.790
Ask them if it was here
when they lived here.

00:11:29.183 --> 00:11:30.228
What, Sari?

00:11:31.016 --> 00:11:32.739
The thing in my closet.

00:11:32.769 --> 00:11:37.056
Oh, no, baby, there was
nothing in their closets.

00:11:37.209 --> 00:11:38.011
Right?

00:11:38.836 --> 00:11:41.083
Right, no.No, of course not.

00:11:42.345 --> 00:11:44.958
She had a nightmare the other night.

00:11:45.073 --> 00:11:46.586
I wasn't dreaming.

00:11:46.770 --> 00:11:50.186
It came into my bedroom,
and it was on fire.

00:11:51.179 --> 00:11:54.114
You heard that ? A figure on fire.

00:11:54.437 --> 00:11:56.785
And that woman Jenny, that was
the woman in your dreams? Yeah.

00:11:56.857 --> 00:11:59.607
And you hear what she was talking
about ? Scratching, flickering lights ?

00:11:59.683 --> 00:12:01.907
Both signs of a malevolent
spirit. Yeah well.

00:12:02.022 --> 00:12:04.161
I'm just freaked out your
weirdo visions are coming true.

00:12:04.177 --> 00:12:05.347
Forget about that for a minute.

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:08.213
The thing in the house, do you think it's the
thing that killed mom and Jessica? I don't know!

00:12:08.439 --> 00:12:10.474
Has it come back or has it
been there the whole time?

00:12:10.479 --> 00:12:12.824
Maybe it's something else
entirely. Sam, we don't know yet.

00:12:12.833 --> 00:12:14.607
Those people are in danger, Dean.

00:12:15.023 --> 00:12:16.992
We have to get them out
of that house. And we will.

00:12:17.022 --> 00:12:18.832
No, I mean now. And how
you're gonna do that ?

00:12:18.849 --> 00:12:21.477
You got a story she's gonna believe?
Then what are we supposed to do?!

00:12:22.013 --> 00:12:23.741
We just got to chill out, that's all.

00:12:24.596 --> 00:12:26.953
If this was any other kind
of job, what would we do?

00:12:32.052 --> 00:12:33.949
We'd try to figure out
what we were dealing with.

00:12:34.503 --> 00:12:37.042
We'd dig into the history
of the house. Exactly.

00:12:37.065 --> 00:12:38.601
Except this time we
already know what happened.

00:12:38.634 --> 00:12:42.230
Yeah, but how much do we know?
How much do you actually remember?

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:46.118
About that night, you mean? Yeah.

00:12:48.063 --> 00:12:49.032
Not much.

00:12:50.484 --> 00:12:51.849
I remember the fire...

00:12:52.847 --> 00:12:53.742
The heat.

00:12:57.662 --> 00:12:59.158
Then I carried you out the front door.

00:13:01.902 --> 00:13:02.739
You did?

00:13:04.559 --> 00:13:05.982
Yeah, well, you never knew that?

00:13:08.309 --> 00:13:09.150
No.

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:12.088
And, uh...

00:13:12.161 --> 00:13:14.641
Well, you know dad's story
as well as I do. Mom was...

00:13:16.182 --> 00:13:17.253
Was on the ceiling.

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:20.555
Whatever put her there was long
gone by the time dad found her.

00:13:21.583 --> 00:13:24.277
And he never had a
theory about what did it?

00:13:24.782 --> 00:13:26.353
If he did, he kept it to himself.

00:13:27.264 --> 00:13:29.538
God knows we asked him enough times.

00:13:32.488 --> 00:13:33.324
Okay.

00:13:34.235 --> 00:13:36.744
So, if we're gonna figure
out what's going on now,

00:13:38.109 --> 00:13:39.914
We have to figure out
what happened back then,

00:13:41.191 --> 00:13:42.790
And see if it's the same thing.

00:13:42.952 --> 00:13:43.421
Yeah.

00:13:44.815 --> 00:13:47.904
Talk to dad's friends, neighbors,
people who were there at the time.

00:13:49.824 --> 00:13:52.125
Does this feel like
just another job to you?

00:13:58.824 --> 00:14:00.599
I'll be right back. I
got to go to the bathroom.

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:20.922
<i>This is John Winchester.</i>

00:14:20.994 --> 00:14:27.289
<i>If this is an emergency, call
my son Dean, 866 907 32 35.</i>

00:14:27.333 --> 00:14:27.847
Dad...

00:14:31.062 --> 00:14:33.515
I know I've left you messages before.

00:14:34.760 --> 00:14:36.442
I don't even know if you get 'em.

00:14:39.441 --> 00:14:39.999
But

00:14:40.469 --> 00:14:41.584
I'm with Sam

00:14:42.626 --> 00:14:44.167
And we're in Lawrence,

00:14:45.179 --> 00:14:47.607
And there's something in our old house.

00:14:48.936 --> 00:14:51.688
I don't know if it's the
thing that killed mom or not,

00:14:53.151 --> 00:14:53.576
But...

00:14:56.100 --> 00:14:57.982
I don't know what to do.

00:14:59.901 --> 00:15:00.679
So,

00:15:01.031 --> 00:15:03.293
Whatever you're doing,
if you could get here...

00:15:05.257 --> 00:15:06.123
Please.

00:15:08.751 --> 00:15:10.204
I need your help, dad.

00:15:15.282 --> 00:15:18.862
No, sir, nothing weird
down there. I promise.

00:15:19.361 --> 00:15:22.311
Sink just backed upon
its own. I'll take a look.

00:15:22.502 --> 00:15:23.426
Thanks.

00:15:24.556 --> 00:15:26.699
Oh, okay, I'll get out of your way.

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:12.743
So you and John Winchester, you
used to own this garage together?

00:17:12.816 --> 00:17:15.502
Yeah, we used to. A long time ago.

00:17:15.615 --> 00:17:16.495
Matter of fact,

00:17:16.715 --> 00:17:19.665
Must be 20 years since John disappeared.

00:17:19.809 --> 00:17:21.593
So, why are the cops
interested all of a sudden?

00:17:21.668 --> 00:17:25.660
Oh, we're reopening some of our unsolved cases,
and the Winchester disappearance is one of them.

00:17:25.754 --> 00:17:28.358
Uh-Huh. Well, what do you
want to know about John?

00:17:28.452 --> 00:17:30.692
Whatever you remember, you know.
Whatever sticks out in your mind.

00:17:34.228 --> 00:17:36.888
He was a stubborn
bastard. I remember that.

00:17:37.862 --> 00:17:39.059
And, uh...

00:17:39.117 --> 00:17:42.015
Oh, whatever the game, he
hated to lose, you know?

00:17:42.050 --> 00:17:43.786
It was that whole marine thing.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:45.792
But, uh...

00:17:46.093 --> 00:17:47.536
Well, he sure loved Mary,

00:17:48.545 --> 00:17:50.034
And he doted on those kids.

00:17:50.515 --> 00:17:51.993
But that was before the fire.

00:17:53.081 --> 00:17:53.727
That's right.

00:17:54.043 --> 00:17:55.427
He ever talk about that night?

00:17:57.011 --> 00:17:57.606
No,

00:17:57.981 --> 00:17:59.025
Not at first.

00:17:59.717 --> 00:18:01.571
I think he was in shock. Right,

00:18:02.134 --> 00:18:03.529
But eventually,

00:18:04.597 --> 00:18:05.977
What did he say about it?

00:18:06.667 --> 00:18:09.504
Oh, he wasn't thinking
straight. He said, uh...

00:18:10.128 --> 00:18:13.613
He said something caused
that fire and killed Mary.

00:18:13.648 --> 00:18:14.678
He ever say what did it?

00:18:15.617 --> 00:18:18.136
Nothing did it. It was an accident.

00:18:18.537 --> 00:18:22.208
An electrical short in the
ceiling or walls or something.

00:18:24.156 --> 00:18:27.959
I begged him to get some
help, but... But what?

00:18:28.520 --> 00:18:30.385
Oh, it just got worse and worse.

00:18:30.596 --> 00:18:31.135
How?

00:18:31.863 --> 00:18:35.382
Oh, he started reading
these strange old books.

00:18:35.417 --> 00:18:38.132
He started going to see
this palm reader in town.

00:18:38.305 --> 00:18:40.427
Palm reader? You have a name?

00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:42.479
No.

00:18:46.598 --> 00:18:50.030
All right, so, there are a few
psychics and palm readers in town.

00:18:50.065 --> 00:18:52.510
There's someone named
El Divino. There's...

00:18:52.675 --> 00:18:55.443
There's the mysterious Mr. Fortinsky.

00:18:55.559 --> 00:18:58.198
Uh, Missouri Moseley,
some dude -- Wait, wait...

00:18:58.281 --> 00:18:59.407
Missouri Moseley?

00:18:59.735 --> 00:19:00.193
What?

00:19:00.509 --> 00:19:01.424
That's a psychic?

00:19:02.034 --> 00:19:04.732
Uh...yeah.Yeah, I guess so.

00:19:08.359 --> 00:19:09.263
In dad's journal...

00:19:12.653 --> 00:19:13.927
Look at this.

00:19:15.555 --> 00:19:17.957
First page, first sentence. Read that.

00:19:18.902 --> 00:19:20.228
"I went to Missouri...

00:19:21.483 --> 00:19:23.060
And I learned the truth."

00:19:23.887 --> 00:19:25.699
I always thought he meant the state.

00:19:31.511 --> 00:19:32.989
All right, then.

00:19:33.388 --> 00:19:35.347
Don't you worry about a thing.

00:19:36.156 --> 00:19:37.904
Your wife is crazy about you.

00:19:41.321 --> 00:19:43.959
Whew! Poor bastard.

00:19:44.463 --> 00:19:46.774
His woman cold-Bangin'the gardener.

00:19:47.930 --> 00:19:49.809
Why didn't you tell him?

00:19:50.203 --> 00:19:52.369
People don't come here for the truth.

00:19:52.404 --> 00:19:54.232
They come for good news.

00:19:55.739 --> 00:19:56.537
Well?

00:19:56.701 --> 00:19:59.960
Sam and Dean, come on
already. I ain't got all day.

00:20:08.075 --> 00:20:09.753
Well, let me look at you.

00:20:11.477 --> 00:20:14.493
Oh, you boys grew up handsome.

00:20:14.820 --> 00:20:17.973
And you were one
goofy-Looking kid, too.

00:20:19.732 --> 00:20:20.765
Sam.

00:20:23.685 --> 00:20:25.163
Oh, honey.

00:20:27.052 --> 00:20:30.219
I'm sorry about your girlfriend.

00:20:30.829 --> 00:20:32.465
And your father

00:20:34.157 --> 00:20:35.681
he's missing?

00:20:38.614 --> 00:20:40.248
How'd you know all that?

00:20:40.283 --> 00:20:40.890
Well,

00:20:41.957 --> 00:20:44.840
You were just thinking it, just now.

00:20:45.361 --> 00:20:47.279
Well, where is he? Is he okay?

00:20:47.907 --> 00:20:49.318
I don't know.

00:20:49.983 --> 00:20:50.992
Don't know?

00:20:52.059 --> 00:20:53.775
You're supposed to be a psychic, right?

00:20:54.441 --> 00:20:58.542
Boy, you see me sawing
some bony tramp in half?

00:20:58.577 --> 00:20:59.974
You think I'm a magician?

00:21:00.212 --> 00:21:03.325
I may be able to read thoughts
and sense energies in a room,

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:05.548
But I can't just pull
facts out of thin air.

00:21:05.583 --> 00:21:06.021
Sit!

00:21:06.274 --> 00:21:06.904
Please.

00:21:16.994 --> 00:21:20.630
Boy, you put your foot on my coffee
table, I'm gonna whack you with a spoon.

00:21:20.665 --> 00:21:21.568
I didn't do anything.

00:21:21.653 --> 00:21:23.146
Well, you were thinking about it.

00:21:29.749 --> 00:21:31.384
Okay, so...

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:33.140
Our dad.

00:21:34.004 --> 00:21:35.461
When did you first meet him?

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:37.549
He came for a reading

00:21:38.245 --> 00:21:40.996
A few days after the fire.

00:21:41.884 --> 00:21:45.242
I just told him what was
really out there in the dark.

00:21:45.387 --> 00:21:47.108
I guess you could say

00:21:48.374 --> 00:21:50.467
I drew back the curtains for him.

00:21:50.493 --> 00:21:51.573
What about the fire?

00:21:52.991 --> 00:21:55.633
Do you know about what killed our mom?

00:21:55.870 --> 00:21:56.734
A little.

00:21:57.674 --> 00:21:59.819
Your daddy took me to your house.

00:21:59.993 --> 00:22:01.771
He was hoping I could

00:22:01.916 --> 00:22:02.977
Sense the

00:22:03.446 --> 00:22:04.451
Echoes,

00:22:04.489 --> 00:22:06.507
The fingerprints of this thing.

00:22:06.865 --> 00:22:07.812
And could you?

00:22:08.393 --> 00:22:09.163
I don't...

00:22:10.954 --> 00:22:11.893
What was it?

00:22:12.578 --> 00:22:13.555
I don't know.

00:22:16.410 --> 00:22:18.251
But it was evil.

00:22:18.463 --> 00:22:22.858
Look, I feel just awful
about the poor man's hand,

00:22:23.851 --> 00:22:26.521
But how can I be held liable?

00:22:28.884 --> 00:22:29.467
Yeah, but

00:22:29.626 --> 00:22:31.730
I can't afford a lawyer.

00:22:34.181 --> 00:22:36.892
Okay, listen, y-You just
got to let me call you back.

00:22:38.067 --> 00:22:41.108
Richie, mommy's gonna be right back,

00:22:41.333 --> 00:22:42.075
Okay?

00:22:42.169 --> 00:22:43.014
Okay.

00:22:43.437 --> 00:22:44.064
Okay.

00:22:48.177 --> 00:22:49.135
So,

00:22:50.683 --> 00:22:53.383
You think something's
back in that house?

00:22:54.348 --> 00:22:55.877
Definitely.

00:22:59.013 --> 00:23:00.813
I don't understand.

00:23:01.386 --> 00:23:02.540
What?

00:23:05.199 --> 00:23:07.011
I haven't been back inside,

00:23:07.046 --> 00:23:11.443
But I've been keeping an eye on
the place, and it's been quiet.

00:23:11.687 --> 00:23:13.786
No sudden deaths, no

00:23:13.947 --> 00:23:15.665
Freak accidents.

00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:17.288
Why is it acting up now?

00:23:17.779 --> 00:23:18.633
I don't know.

00:23:19.370 --> 00:23:22.726
But dad going missing
and Jessica dying and

00:23:23.123 --> 00:23:24.677
Now this house,

00:23:25.188 --> 00:23:28.597
All happening at once. It just
feels like something's starting.

00:23:29.267 --> 00:23:31.392
That's a comforting thought.

00:24:02.438 --> 00:24:03.763
Juicy!

00:24:18.150 --> 00:24:22.031
Oh, baby, either we have
rats or mommy is going crazy.

00:24:22.745 --> 00:24:23.495
Richie?

00:24:26.229 --> 00:24:27.366
Richie?!

00:24:37.659 --> 00:24:39.997
Baby, where are you?!

00:24:48.328 --> 00:24:49.008
Wha...

00:24:57.117 --> 00:24:59.299
Mum! Oh, my god!

00:25:05.488 --> 00:25:06.661
Oh, baby!

00:25:09.724 --> 00:25:11.461
Sam, Dean,

00:25:11.836 --> 00:25:13.009
What are you doing here?

00:25:13.185 --> 00:25:14.276
Hey, Jenny.

00:25:14.546 --> 00:25:16.909
Um, this is our friend Missouri.

00:25:17.731 --> 00:25:21.068
If it's not too much trouble, we were
hoping to show her the house, you know,

00:25:21.231 --> 00:25:23.139
For old time's sake.

00:25:23.174 --> 00:25:25.428
No, you know, this isn't a good time.

00:25:25.463 --> 00:25:27.424
I'm kind of busy. Listen,
Jenny,it's important.

00:25:27.569 --> 00:25:28.058
Ow!

00:25:28.419 --> 00:25:31.738
Give the poor girl a break.
Can't you see she's upset?

00:25:31.773 --> 00:25:33.204
Forgive this boy. He means well.

00:25:33.239 --> 00:25:35.275
He's just not the
sharpest tool in the shed.

00:25:35.310 --> 00:25:36.691
But hear me out.

00:25:37.295 --> 00:25:38.401
About what?

00:25:38.459 --> 00:25:39.725
About this house.

00:25:40.520 --> 00:25:41.902
What are you talking about?

00:25:42.397 --> 00:25:45.125
I think you know what I'm talking about.

00:25:45.160 --> 00:25:50.091
You think there's something in this house,
something that wants to hurt your family.

00:25:50.126 --> 00:25:51.580
Am I mistaken?

00:25:52.514 --> 00:25:54.251
Who are you?

00:25:54.286 --> 00:25:57.554
We're people who can help,
who can stop this thing,

00:25:57.589 --> 00:26:00.042
But you're gonna have to
trust us, just a little.

00:26:02.764 --> 00:26:07.968
If there's a dark energy around here,
this room should be the center of it.

00:26:09.317 --> 00:26:10.128
Why?

00:26:10.658 --> 00:26:13.335
This used to be your nursery, Sam.

00:26:13.370 --> 00:26:15.646
This is where it all happened.

00:26:30.935 --> 00:26:32.612
That an emf?

00:26:33.006 --> 00:26:33.592
Yeah.

00:26:34.552 --> 00:26:35.399
Amateur.

00:26:45.764 --> 00:26:48.602
I don't know if you boys should
be disappointed or relieved,

00:26:48.637 --> 00:26:50.818
But this ain't the
thing that took your mom.

00:26:52.478 --> 00:26:53.906
Are you sure?

00:26:54.887 --> 00:26:56.113
How do you know?

00:26:56.119 --> 00:26:59.921
It isn't the same energy I
felt the last time I was here.

00:26:59.956 --> 00:27:01.368
It's something different.

00:27:02.353 --> 00:27:03.375
What is it?

00:27:05.004 --> 00:27:06.495
Not it...

00:27:07.253 --> 00:27:08.797
Them.

00:27:09.411 --> 00:27:12.478
There's more than one
spirit in this place.

00:27:13.634 --> 00:27:15.246
What are they doing here?

00:27:15.281 --> 00:27:18.140
They're here because of
what happened to your family.

00:27:18.734 --> 00:27:20.636
You see, all those years ago,

00:27:20.728 --> 00:27:23.268
Real evil came to you.

00:27:24.648 --> 00:27:29.242
It walked this house. That
kind of evil leaves wounds,

00:27:29.277 --> 00:27:32.050
And sometimes wounds get infected.

00:27:32.366 --> 00:27:34.098
I don't understand.

00:27:34.133 --> 00:27:37.408
This place is a magnet
for paranormal energy.

00:27:40.222 --> 00:27:42.632
It's attracted a poltergeist,

00:27:43.087 --> 00:27:44.760
A nasty one,

00:27:45.527 --> 00:27:49.288
And it won't rest until
Jenny and her babies are dead.

00:27:49.323 --> 00:27:51.552
You said there was more than one spirit.

00:27:51.641 --> 00:27:53.144
There is.

00:27:56.004 --> 00:27:59.301
I just can't quite
make out the second one.

00:28:03.361 --> 00:28:05.205
Well, one thing's for damn sure,

00:28:05.793 --> 00:28:07.630
Nobody's dying in this house,

00:28:07.665 --> 00:28:08.804
Ever again.

00:28:09.484 --> 00:28:11.835
So, whatever is here, how do we stop it?

00:28:15.249 --> 00:28:17.370
So, what is all this stuff anyway?

00:28:17.811 --> 00:28:21.250
Angelica root, van van
oil, crossroad dirt,

00:28:21.305 --> 00:28:23.241
A few other odds and ends.

00:28:23.276 --> 00:28:24.505
What are we supposed to do with it?

00:28:24.540 --> 00:28:27.712
We're gonna put them inside the walls

00:28:27.928 --> 00:28:31.160
In the north, south, east, west corners

00:28:31.195 --> 00:28:33.127
On each floor of the house.

00:28:33.162 --> 00:28:36.270
Punching holes in the drywall.
Jenny's gonna love that.

00:28:37.230 --> 00:28:38.647
She'll live.

00:28:39.715 --> 00:28:41.958
And this will destroy the spirits?

00:28:41.993 --> 00:28:43.270
It should.

00:28:43.840 --> 00:28:46.461
It should purify the house completely.

00:28:47.604 --> 00:28:49.270
We'll each take a floor,

00:28:49.633 --> 00:28:51.143
But we work fast.

00:28:51.178 --> 00:28:54.039
Once the spirits
realize what we're up to,

00:28:54.067 --> 00:28:56.198
Things are gonna get bad.

00:28:57.969 --> 00:28:58.821
Okay.

00:29:00.151 --> 00:29:01.534
Careful.

00:29:03.037 --> 00:29:06.847
Look, I -You know, I'm not sure I'm
comfortable leaving you guys here alone.

00:29:06.882 --> 00:29:09.181
Just take your kids to
the movie or something, and

00:29:09.219 --> 00:29:11.373
It'll be over by the time you get back.

00:29:12.245 --> 00:29:12.937
Okay.

00:30:09.621 --> 00:30:11.372
Aah! Uhh!

00:30:49.430 --> 00:30:50.205
Sam!

00:30:52.516 --> 00:30:53.255
Sam!

00:31:16.277 --> 00:31:17.469
Come on.

00:31:39.245 --> 00:31:41.130
Are you sure this is over?

00:31:44.299 --> 00:31:45.609
I'm sure.

00:31:46.037 --> 00:31:46.646
Why?

00:31:47.796 --> 00:31:49.483
Why do you ask?

00:31:50.338 --> 00:31:51.929
No, never mind.

00:31:53.634 --> 00:31:55.481
It's nothing, I guess.

00:31:57.517 --> 00:31:58.840
Hello?

00:31:59.417 --> 00:32:00.896
We're home.

00:32:03.933 --> 00:32:05.541
What happened?

00:32:05.645 --> 00:32:08.316
Hi. Sorry. Um, we'll...

00:32:08.351 --> 00:32:10.381
We'll pay for all of this.

00:32:11.143 --> 00:32:12.575
Don't you worry.

00:32:12.633 --> 00:32:14.698
Dean's gonna clean up this mess.

00:32:17.724 --> 00:32:19.707
Well, what are you waiting for, boy?

00:32:19.742 --> 00:32:20.510
Get the mop.

00:32:21.414 --> 00:32:22.974
And don't cuss at me.

00:32:44.504 --> 00:32:45.267
Okay.

00:33:39.226 --> 00:33:41.331
So, tell me again. What
are we still doing here?

00:33:41.366 --> 00:33:42.827
I don't know, I-I just...

00:33:43.472 --> 00:33:45.056
I still have a bad feeling.

00:33:45.642 --> 00:33:46.651
Why?

00:33:47.167 --> 00:33:50.812
Missouri did her whole zelda rubenstein thing.
The house should be clean. This should be over.

00:33:51.037 --> 00:33:53.946
Yeah, probably, but I just
want to make sure. That's all.

00:33:55.410 --> 00:33:58.466
The problem is I could be
sleeping in a bed right now.

00:34:02.837 --> 00:34:03.775
Dean!

00:34:04.256 --> 00:34:04.956
Dean!

00:34:06.915 --> 00:34:08.759
You grab the kids, I'll get Jenny.

00:34:27.418 --> 00:34:29.119
Come on! Jenny!

00:34:29.157 --> 00:34:31.775
I can't open the door! Stand back!

00:34:34.841 --> 00:34:36.342
Come on! No, my kids!

00:34:36.349 --> 00:34:37.469
Sam's got your kids. Come on.

00:34:40.221 --> 00:34:41.315
Help!

00:34:41.972 --> 00:34:43.086
Please!

00:34:46.699 --> 00:34:47.813
Come here.

00:34:48.514 --> 00:34:50.106
Don't look, don't look.

00:35:03.454 --> 00:35:06.742
Sari, take your brother outside as
fast as you can and don't look back.

00:35:15.028 --> 00:35:16.617
Are you okay, baby?

00:35:16.640 --> 00:35:19.500
Sari, where's Sam? He's
inside. Something's got him.

00:35:41.772 --> 00:35:43.694
Ugh! Aah!

00:36:06.741 --> 00:36:07.319
Sam!

00:36:28.050 --> 00:36:28.881
Sam?!

00:36:29.782 --> 00:36:30.307
Sam!

00:36:35.062 --> 00:36:37.200
No, don't! Don't! What? Why?

00:36:38.513 --> 00:36:39.993
Because I know who it is.

00:36:40.769 --> 00:36:42.487
I can see her now.

00:36:59.613 --> 00:37:00.949
Mom.

00:37:11.264 --> 00:37:12.569
Dean.

00:37:27.916 --> 00:37:29.366
Sam.

00:37:35.844 --> 00:37:37.501
I'm sorry.

00:37:42.221 --> 00:37:43.883
F-For what?

00:37:56.190 --> 00:37:59.055
You, get out of my house.

00:37:59.872 --> 00:38:02.191
And let go of my son.

00:38:32.398 --> 00:38:33.970
Now it's over.

00:38:47.689 --> 00:38:48.943
Thanks for these.

00:38:49.455 --> 00:38:51.558
Don't thank me. They're yours.

00:38:56.269 --> 00:38:57.143
Well,

00:38:57.622 --> 00:39:01.218
There are no spirits in there
anymore, this time for sure.

00:39:02.402 --> 00:39:04.075
Not even my mom?

00:39:04.740 --> 00:39:06.075
No.

00:39:10.432 --> 00:39:11.921
What happened?

00:39:12.968 --> 00:39:17.625
Your mom's spirit and the poltergeists'
energy, they canceled each other out.

00:39:18.115 --> 00:39:21.704
Your mom destroyed herself
going after the thing.

00:39:22.961 --> 00:39:25.222
Why would she do something like that?

00:39:26.270 --> 00:39:29.349
Well, to protect her boys, of course.

00:39:37.224 --> 00:39:39.220
Sam, I'm sorry.

00:39:41.573 --> 00:39:42.963
For what?

00:39:43.493 --> 00:39:46.355
You sensed it was here, didn't you?

00:39:46.390 --> 00:39:48.115
Even when I couldn't.

00:39:53.123 --> 00:39:54.874
What's happening to me?

00:39:55.837 --> 00:39:58.839
I know I should have
all the answers, but...

00:40:00.540 --> 00:40:01.967
I don't know.

00:40:02.541 --> 00:40:03.984
Sam, you ready ?

00:40:09.044 --> 00:40:10.174
Bye.

00:40:13.167 --> 00:40:14.542
Bye Sam.

00:40:17.053 --> 00:40:18.213
Ah.

00:40:18.894 --> 00:40:21.235
Don't you boys be strangers.

00:40:21.658 --> 00:40:22.891
We won't.

00:40:24.438 --> 00:40:25.692
See you around.

00:40:56.999 --> 00:40:58.596
That boy...

00:41:00.228 --> 00:41:02.108
He has such

00:41:02.200 --> 00:41:04.195
Powerful abilities.

00:41:07.970 --> 00:41:10.707
Why he couldn't sense his own father,

00:41:10.919 --> 00:41:12.537
I have no idea.

00:41:18.289 --> 00:41:19.426
Mary's spirit...

00:41:21.219 --> 00:41:23.521
Do you really think she saved the boys?

00:41:25.860 --> 00:41:26.809
I do.

00:41:38.792 --> 00:41:41.515
John Winchester, I could just slap you.

00:41:41.581 --> 00:41:44.035
Why don't you go talk to your children?

00:41:45.667 --> 00:41:47.179
God, I want to.

00:41:49.164 --> 00:41:51.662
You have no idea how
much I want to see them.

00:41:54.602 --> 00:41:55.556
But I can't.

00:41:57.218 --> 00:41:57.923
Not yet.

00:42:04.463 --> 00:42:06.238
Not until I know the truth.



00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.000
